{"id": "c0d1629a-9ce1-4ff6-891f-ccfde86fccdf", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit the CloudTrail setup in account 012345678901. That covers trails, event selectors, log destinations, and what isn't covered. I'm running it read-only and checking every region.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_bj4REx58qIEKfCN2psRTci", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cloudtrail-config-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "verifying-with-docs", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "[DEEP RESEARCH MODE]
{
  "task": "Produce an audit-grade, READ-ONLY report of the CloudTrail configuration in AWS account 012345678901, stating exactly what is and is NOT being captured.",
  "context": "Customer's auditors need a precise statement of CloudTrail coverage. Do not make any mutating calls. Use only describe/get/list CloudTrail-configuration APIs (through whatever route is available; if use_aws blocks CloudTrail, say so and use the alternatives from the investigating-infrastructure-changes skill and other services such as S3/KMS/CloudWatch Logs/SNS/Config/EventBridge). Check ALL enabled regions (use ec2 describe_regions, and note opt-in regions status), starting from us-east-1. State clearly any check you could not perform (e.g. permission denied) rather than guessing.",
  "resources": ["AWS_ACCOUNT:012345678901"],
  "criteria": "For every region and trail (including shadow trails of multi-region trails and organization trails): (1) list_trails/describe_trails: name, home region, IsMultiRegionTrail, IsOrganizationTrail, IncludeGlobalServiceEvents, S3 bucket + prefix, KMS key, SNS topic, CloudWatch Logs group/role, LogFileValidationEnabled; (2) get_trail_status: IsLogging, LatestDeliveryTime, LatestDeliveryError, LatestDigestDeliveryTime, StartLoggingTime/StopLoggingTime; (3) get_event_selectors incl. advanced event selectors: management events (ReadWriteType, exclusions such as KMS/RDS Data API), data events (S3, Lambda, DynamoDB, other resource types) and which resources/buckets are covered, Insights selectors (get_insights_selectors), network activity events if present; (4) CloudTrail Lake event data stores (list_event_data_stores) and their selectors, retention, termination protection, and any channels; (5) destination S3 bucket posture: bucket policy for cloudtrail, versioning, MFA delete, object lock, lifecycle/retention, encryption, public access block, access logging, cross-account/replication; KMS key policy allowing CloudTrail and rotation; (6) CloudWatch Logs group retention and metric filters/alarms for key events (root login, console login without MFA, IAM policy changes, CloudTrail config changes, unauthorized API calls, security group/NACL/route changes); (7) regions with NO logging trail coverage; whether global service events (IAM, STS, CloudFront) are captured and by which trail; (8) GAPS: S3 buckets/Lambda functions/DynamoDB tables in the account NOT covered by data event selectors (enumerate S3 buckets and compare), read-only management events excluded, Insights not enabled, trails not logging, delivery errors, trails with no log file validation, no encryption, etc.; (9) recent CloudTrail configuration changes (StopLogging, DeleteTrail, UpdateTrail, PutEventSelectors) in the last 90 days if the CloudTrail event lookup is available; (10) whether AWS Config/Security Hub CloudTrail-related checks exist, if easily available. Output: a structured report with a per-trail table, a clear 'CAPTURED' list, a clear 'NOT CAPTURED / GAPS' list, severity-ranked findings, and an explicit list of checks that could not be completed and why. Include the exact timestamp of when the audit was performed."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail configuration across regions (read-only)"}], "created_at": null}

